+# Sweep the settled tasks off the board. Every worker leaves a task; a worker that dies
+# mid-run leaves it in ready/blocked forever, and nothing in the merge path revisited it —
+# the board grew to 37 "open" tasks for work that had landed. sweep.sh closes only the
+# unambiguous ones (names a merged PR / closed issue) and never touches a live dispatch.
